<section class="section" id="institutions">
  <div class="conteneur">
    <h2>For a school, a company or a public body</h2>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>AZERTY Global installs without an account or a network dependency, and computers keep
      their existing AZERTY alongside it: each person switches from one to the other when
      they decide to.</p>
      <p>The AMCF publishes the code under the EUPL&nbsp;1.2 license, signs the packages intended
      for organizations, and provides the printable cheat sheet and a getting-started course. The
      AMCF supports schools and public administrations that deploy AZERTY Global free of charge,
      starting with a <a href="/pilote" hreflang="fr">pilot on a few computers<span class="visuellement-cache"> (in French)</span></a>.</p>
    </div>

    <details class="notice">
      <summary>How a deployment works</summary>
      <div class="notice__contenu prose">
        <p>In practice, an IT department deploys the signed MSIX kit like any other application in
        its fleet, with no account or network dependency; the EXE installer, for its part, adds the
        layout to Windows’ language options. There is no migration to plan and no rollback to
        prepare: you uninstall AZERTY Global the way you installed it. That is why adoption can
        go computer by computer, department by department, without a company-wide project.</p>
        <p>Published in the <em>Journal officiel des associations</em> of 7&nbsp;April&nbsp;2026,
        the association designs and distributes free keyboard layouts, produces the educational
        resources that go with them and works to make them known to schools, companies and
        institutions.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="etapes-suivantes">
      <a href="/entreprises" class="etape-suivante" hreflang="fr">
