<section class="section" id="faq">
  <div class="conteneur">
    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

    <details class="notice" id="layout">
      <summary>What is a keyboard layout?</summary>
      <div class="notice__contenu prose">
        <p>The keyboard only reports which key is pressed; it is the layout, on the software side,
        that decides which character appears. Changing the layout therefore changes what each key
        produces, without touching the hardware.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="notice" id="adjustment-time">
      <summary>How long does it take to get used to it?</summary>
      <div class="notice__contenu prose">
        <p>A few days of use for the reflexes to settle in. The letters A to Z, the digits and the
        home row landmarks stay in place; what takes some adjustment is the five changes and the
        habit of using <kbd>AltGr</kbd> for the new characters. The printable cheat sheet in the
        <a href="/en/guide">guide</a> fits on one A4 page.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="notice" id="new-keyboard">
      <summary>Do I need to buy a keyboard?</summary>
      <div class="notice__contenu prose">
        <p>No. AZERTY Global is a software layout: it changes what each key produces, not what is
        printed on it. Your current keyboard works. Key stickers are possible for the added
        characters, but not necessary.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="notice" id="games">
      <summary>Is it compatible with games and shortcuts?</summary>
      <div class="notice__contenu prose">
        <p>For <kbd>Z</kbd> <kbd>Q</kbd> <kbd>S</kbd> <kbd>D</kbd> movement, yes: the letters A to
        Z stay in place, and <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> shortcuts are unchanged. Some games, however, depend
        on the console key, a shortcut or an anti-cheat system:
        <a href="/en/compatibility">the compatibility page</a> lists the known cases.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <div class="prose questions-accueil__tout">
      <p><a href="/en/faq">All frequently asked questions</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

